course: dictionary
lesson: 8490
title: Sandstone, a rock made of sand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sandstone is a rock. Its name tells you what it is made of: sand. Tiny grains of sand get pressed together and stuck together over a very, very long time, until they form solid rock. «Sandstone is made of sand grains cemented together, often from old beaches, rivers or deserts.»
explain: Look for the clues in a sentence. «Sedimentary rock forms from layers of sand, mud or shells pressed together.» Sedimentary is a long word, but the clues are layers, pressed together, sand, mud and shells. So a sedimentary rock is built up in layers, and sandstone is one of them.
explain: You can often see the layers in sandstone, like the pages of a book. Sandstone is a good word to know in geography too: many cliffs and buildings are made of it, and Uluru in Australia is a giant sandstone rock.
fact: Sandstone is a sedimentary rock.
fact: Sandstone is made of sand grains pressed and stuck together.
fact: The sand in sandstone often came from old beaches, rivers or deserts.
fact: Sandstone often shows layers, like the pages of a book.
fact: Uluru in Australia is a giant sandstone rock.
exercise: What is sandstone? | A soft, fluffy kind of cloud | *A rock made of sand grains pressed and stuck together | A metal dug out of mines | A wood used to make furniture
exercise: «Sandstone is made of sand grains cemented together, often from old beaches, rivers or deserts.» Where does the sand often come from? | Ice caves in the mountains | *Old beaches, rivers or deserts | Volcanoes on the moon | Busy shopping centres
exercise: «Sedimentary rock forms from layers of sand, mud or shells pressed together.» Which of these is a sedimentary rock? | Lava | *Sandstone | Granite | Marble
test: «Sandstone is made of sand grains cemented together.» What does the word sandstone tell you about what it is made of? | Metal and glass | Wood and leaves | *Sand | Water and ice
test: Sandstone is a sedimentary rock, like limestone and chalk. What do all sedimentary rocks form from? | Crystals grown in caves | Ice frozen over many winters | Hot melted rock from volcanoes | *Layers of sand, mud or shells pressed together
exam: Sandstone is a sedimentary rock made of sand grains pressed together. Which sentence is true? | Sandstone forms in a few seconds after a storm | Sandstone is a metal that is found in mines | *Sandstone often shows layers, like the pages of a book | Sandstone is made of melted glass
